Stage 3: the SELECT A CAMPAIGN modal screen (ec7e) render + CAMPAIGNS->OK dispatch wiring.

Clicking OK in the SELECT PLAYER roster reached from CAMPAIGNS now opens FUN_0000_ec7e, the "SELECT A
CAMPAIGN" modal screen: a left LIST of the 7 decrypted campaign names (TRAINING [red-selected] .. BURNING
FROST, parsed by patch 147's ef5e chain), a right HARDWARE group (WESTERN [red] / EASTERN radios), and
OK / CANCEL.  Its first settled frame is bit-identical (AE=0) to a genuine DOSBox capture on native + wasm.

All asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.  The recurring class here is the b941 campaign-name table
walk: `si = word[DGROUP:0xf941 + bx]` yields a DGROUP NEAR-OFFSET that Ghidra dereferenced as a HOST
pointer (fault 0xfffff941).  Rebase every byte read of that offset to g_mem[0x1c000 + (uint16)si]; the
parsed name lives at DGROUP:(si+1).

 - DAT_2000_b848 retyped undefined2 -> uint8_t: ec7e's exit flag is a BYTE (asm `movb [0xf848]`); the WORD
   store at ec7e entry (`DAT_2000_b848 = 0`) clobbered the adjacent HARDWARE-icon rect at DGROUP:0xf849
   (ed14/ee67/eeab draw from 0xf849/0xf812/0xf81a).  0=idle / 1=OK / 0xff=CANCEL.

 - FUN_0000_ec7e (0xec7e): the modal screen.  Fix the b941 walk base-loss (find the first LOADED campaign
   from [0x77d6]); reconstruct the CF-driven modal loop faithfully (mirror the proven cc33 loop, patch 137):
   206f paint -> 3907 -> if g_fist_cf: 096c -> inner poll [DGROUP:0x40a]=35a7 (sets g_fist_cf, patch 073):
   CF=1 (frame due) repaints, CF=0 dispatches events (1e4b) until b848 is set (OK/CANCEL).  Exit CF to the
   caller = (b848==0xff)==CANCEL.  f0f1 (the OK submenu) is unreached on the first frame.

 - FUN_0000_ed28 (0xed28): the campaign-LIST paint method (cdc4-lesson).  Ghidra base-lost the b941 walk and
   DROPPED the selection-bar colour (`al=0xf8 if row==[0x77d6]` -> c60a fill) and the glyph colour
   (`al=0x1f/0x20 from byte[DGROUP:0x77da+row]&0x80` -> c684).  Reconstructed: per LOADED row draw the
   selection bar (c60a), the hardware-type glyph (52d1 setpos + c684), and the NAME (52d1 + the DGROUP-string
   drawstring thunk_FUN_1000_5531 = f69:0x5e9b, patch 139) from DGROUP:(si+1).

 - FUN_0000_edc2 (0xedc2): the list HIT-TEST / row-select.  click Y at [si+4] where si = the drained coord
   node word[DGROUP:0x18e2] (Ghidra bound it to param_2, base-loss, ccde class/patch 142); row = ((Y-0x60)/7)
   *2; if LOADED and != [0x77d6] -> select (b882=3 BYTE dirty, [0x77d6]=row).

 - FUN_0000_ed14 / ee67 / eeab: the HARDWARE box + WESTERN/EASTERN radio-icon PAINT methods.  Ghidra dropped
   the c6b4 sprite/rect args (ax=sprite id, bx=DGROUP rect; c6b4 sig per patch 139).  ed14 -> 0x13e0@0xf849;
   ee67 (WESTERN) -> (DAT_2000_2db4!=0 ? 0x13c8 : 0x13d0)@0xf812; eeab (EASTERN) -> the opposite @0xf81a.

 - FUN_0000_ef39: the campaign-screen KEYBOARD accel handler (off the mouse-driven flow, reconstructed
   faithfully): the scancode is at [si+2], si=word[DGROUP:0x18e2]; match (key&0xf77f) against the 11-entry
   b851 accel table (stride 4) with a 16-bit compare -> near-dispatch.

